WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.152 --> 00:00:20.233
Jack had quit the team three days earlier but still hadn't gotten the nerve to tell his parents.

2
00:00:21.213 --> 00:00:26.335
The last three mornings, after his mother drove him to the community center, Jack walked to a coffee

3
00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:29.596
shop. He bought lemonade there and played games on his phone.

4
00:00:30.704 --> 00:00:35.227
After a couple of hours, he wet his hair in the bathroom sink and went outside to meet

5
00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:35.707
his mom.

6
00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:38.969
The routine was getting boring and lonely.

7
00:00:39.869 --> 00:00:43.491
Today he sat in the coffee shop and called his best friend in Oklahoma.

8
00:00:45.992 --> 00:00:48.514
"Yo!" Noah said.

9
00:00:48.534 --> 00:00:50.155
"Great to hear from you, dude!"

10
00:00:51.135 --> 00:00:51.815
Jack grinned.

11
00:00:51.836 --> 00:00:55.698
"I bet Los Angeles is totally amazing," Noah said.

12
00:00:55.718 --> 00:00:57.599
"How many celebrities have you met?

13
00:00:57.819 --> 00:00:58.579
Have you gone surfing?

14
00:00:58.819 --> 00:00:59.820
Talked to beautiful girls?"

15
00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:05.182
"Zero, no, and yes," Jack replied.

16
00:01:06.023 --> 00:01:08.605
Well, he'd talked to one beautiful girl.

17
00:01:09.145 --> 00:01:11.527
But he hadn't seen Laura since he'd quit the swim team.

18
00:01:11.547 --> 00:01:13.968
"Guess who I went out with last night?"

19
00:01:14.228 --> 00:01:14.689
Noah said.

20
00:01:15.249 --> 00:01:18.071
Before Jack could guess, Noah blurted out the answer.

21
00:01:18.091 --> 00:01:22.734
"Kara. Since you're not around, I asked Kara to the movies."

22
00:01:22.754 --> 00:01:25.016
"Whoa," Jack said.

23
00:01:25.656 --> 00:01:27.357
Neither of them had been on a date before.

24
00:01:27.377 --> 00:01:28.938
"It was great!"

25
00:01:30.099 --> 00:01:31.280
"Awesome!" Jack said.

26
00:01:31.808 --> 00:01:33.830
"Hey, how did the swim meet go?"

27
00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:35.011
"We won.

28
00:01:35.531 --> 00:01:38.514
And I got my personal best time in the backstroke," Noah said.

29
00:01:39.494 --> 00:01:46.740
"Congratulations." "Oh, and now that our best swimmer—you, of course—is gone, I'm doing breaststroke on the relay team."

30
00:01:46.760 --> 00:01:49.523
"Cool," Jack said.

31
00:01:49.543 --> 00:01:52.305
"So you talked to some beautiful girls?"

32
00:01:52.785 --> 00:01:53.326
Noah asked.

33
00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:56.889
"Just one but we swam together at my pool."

34
00:01:56.909 --> 00:01:59.150
"Awesome," Noah said.

35
00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:00.972
"I should ask her out.

36
00:02:01.384 --> 00:02:03.065
If you can get a date, anyone can!"

37
00:02:03.445 --> 00:02:04.085
Jack joked.

38
00:02:05.205 --> 00:02:06.205
Noah laughed along.

39
00:02:06.786 --> 00:02:09.946
"If you weren't so far away, I'd punch you.

40
00:02:10.507 --> 00:02:12.707
So did you totally impress the girl with your swimming?"

41
00:02:12.727 --> 00:02:18.349
"Totally." Jack had lost a race to Laura and done a belly flop in front of her.

42
00:02:19.129 --> 00:02:22.650
So he'd definitely made an impression—an awful one!

43
00:02:22.670 --> 00:02:24.471
"I need to go, Noah.

44
00:02:24.851 --> 00:02:26.351
Congrats on swimming your personal best.

45
00:02:26.671 --> 00:02:27.551
And on dating Kara."

46
00:02:28.212 --> 00:02:31.269
Jack clicked off his phone, feeling lonelier than ever.

47
00:02:32.970 --> 00:02:36.251
Later Jack's mother drove him home from fake swim practice.

48
00:02:37.172 --> 00:02:40.374
Back at the apartment, Luke was playing with one of their new neighbors.

49
00:02:41.254 --> 00:02:44.796
The two little boys ran through the small apartment, waving rubber swords.

50
00:02:47.497 --> 00:02:51.379
Meanwhile the Long-Hair Boys song played over and over through the wall.

51
00:02:59.116 --> 00:03:01.178
Jack clapped his hands over his ears.

52
00:03:01.198 --> 00:03:04.400
"Mom, can I go to the pool?"

53
00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.502
"Aren't you tired from your practice this morning?"

54
00:03:08.503 --> 00:03:09.884
Jack quickly shook his head.

55
00:03:09.904 --> 00:03:11.725
"Nope. I'm feeling great."

56
00:03:12.806 --> 00:03:14.167
"All right," his mother said.

57
00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:18.830
"You know the rule: if you're the only one at the pool, you have to come home."

58
00:03:20.251 --> 00:03:22.473
When Jack got to the pool, he groaned.

59
00:03:24.354 --> 00:03:26.416
He definitely wasn't the only one there.

60
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:29.061
Mrs. Wilson was sitting on a lounge chair.

61
00:03:30.622 --> 00:03:33.543
He forced himself to be polite and waved to her.

62
00:03:34.623 --> 00:03:35.984
She peered at him, frowning.

63
00:03:36.844 --> 00:03:41.506
"Young man, you need to practice if you want to swim faster than your girlfriend."

64
00:03:41.526 --> 00:03:46.568
"She's not my—" "You should be out here every day.

65
00:03:46.948 --> 00:03:52.770
My grandson, little Tommy, once swam 196 days in a row.

66
00:03:53.491 --> 00:03:57.376
He took a few days off only because he got pinkeye."

67
00:03:57.396 --> 00:03:58.537
"Oh," Jack said.

68
00:03:59.137 --> 00:04:00.257
He dived into the pool.

69
00:04:02.678 --> 00:04:04.839
"Streamline! Streamline!

70
00:04:04.919 --> 00:04:06.620
Streamline!" Mrs.

71
00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:07.440
Wilson yelled.

72
00:04:08.341 --> 00:04:12.803
After three laps of the freestyle stroke, Jack stood up at the shallow end of the pool.

73
00:04:17.705 --> 00:04:18.965
your hands more.

74
00:04:19.045 --> 00:04:19.886
Like this."

75
00:04:20.586 --> 00:04:22.227
Mrs. Wilson cupped her hands.

76
00:04:22.247 --> 00:04:24.528
"Thank you, Mrs.

77
00:04:24.568 --> 00:04:29.186
Wilson." Jack sat on the pool steps and closed his eyes for a few moments.

78
00:04:29.206 --> 00:04:33.467
"‘Listen to my pleas.

79
00:04:34.348 --> 00:04:41.571
You're the one for me,'" a girl's voice sang next to him.

80
00:04:42.511 --> 00:04:43.812
Jack's eyes flew open.

81
00:04:44.532 --> 00:04:47.233
Laura was standing over him, at the edge of the pool.

82
00:04:47.933 --> 00:04:50.014
Had he been humming that awful song again?

83
00:04:51.135 --> 00:04:51.875
She grinned at him.

84
00:04:51.895 --> 00:04:53.536
"I love that song!

85
00:04:54.036 --> 00:04:56.198
I saw the Long-Hair Boys in concert last year."

86
00:04:56.218 --> 00:05:01.782
"Oh. That song is Jack tried to think of something good about it.

87
00:05:02.583 --> 00:05:04.385
"Um, it's really catchy."

88
00:05:06.026 --> 00:05:11.010
Laura sat on the pool steps, so close to him he could see the cute freckles on her

89
00:05:11.070 --> 00:05:13.852
cheeks. "How come you haven't been to swim practice?"

90
00:05:14.433 --> 00:05:15.053
Laura asked.

91
00:05:15.073 --> 00:05:21.999
"I uh Jack looked away, wondering what the coach had said to the other swimmers.

92
00:05:23.804 --> 00:05:24.665
"Well, I had pinkeye."

93
00:05:24.685 --> 00:05:26.826
"Too bad," she said.

94
00:05:26.846 --> 00:05:28.087
"Hi, Jack!"

95
00:05:28.507 --> 00:05:29.188
Luke shouted.

96
00:05:29.728 --> 00:05:34.671
Luke and his new friend rushed toward the swimming pool, throwing a beach ball at each other and

97
00:05:34.771 --> 00:05:35.812
squealing happily.

98
00:05:40.295 --> 00:05:41.055
down, boys!"

99
00:05:41.556 --> 00:05:48.000
Mrs. Gibson said, hurrying after them with a large mesh bag filled with towels, water bottles, and sunscreen.

100
00:05:51.492 --> 00:05:53.013
"No running near the pool!

101
00:05:53.293 --> 00:05:54.794
And keep your voices down!"

102
00:05:55.094 --> 00:05:56.075
Mrs. Wilson said.

103
00:05:56.095 --> 00:05:58.676
"Sorry about that," Mrs.

104
00:05:58.736 --> 00:05:59.377
Gibson said.

105
00:05:59.977 --> 00:06:01.518
She introduced herself to Mrs.

106
00:06:01.578 --> 00:06:03.339
Wilson and then looked at Laura.

107
00:06:04.260 --> 00:06:05.020
Laura smiled.

108
00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:07.061
"Hi. I'm Laura Perez.

109
00:06:07.482 --> 00:06:08.742
I live in apartment 2D."

110
00:06:09.423 --> 00:06:10.723
Jack's mother smiled back.

111
00:06:10.743 --> 00:06:13.425
"I'm Anne Marie Gibson.

112
00:06:13.685 --> 00:06:14.466
Nice to meet you."

113
00:06:14.486 --> 00:06:18.108
"Jack and I are on the same swim team," Laura said.

114
00:06:19.028 --> 00:06:21.630
"My mother was wondering if you'd like to carpool to practices."

115
00:06:22.691 --> 00:06:23.932
Jack's heart sank.

116
00:06:24.933 --> 00:06:26.614
He hadn't thought about carpooling!

117
00:06:28.196 --> 00:06:32.239
"It's too bad Jack got pinkeye and missed the last three practices," Laura said.

118
00:06:33.220 --> 00:06:33.960
"Oh no!"

119
00:06:34.261 --> 00:06:34.881
Jack thought.

120
00:06:35.442 --> 00:06:37.283
He couldn't manage to look at his mom.

121
00:06:37.303 --> 00:06:39.345
"What?" Mrs.

122
00:06:39.385 --> 00:06:40.626
Gibson sounded shocked.

123
00:06:40.646 --> 00:06:42.527
"Jack didn't have pinkeye.

124
00:06:43.148 --> 00:06:45.270
He's been at practice every morning this week."

125
00:06:46.351 --> 00:06:47.732
Laura shot a look at Jack.

126
00:06:48.736 --> 00:06:50.137
Jack's mother looked at him too.

127
00:06:50.157 --> 00:06:53.198
"You have been going to practice, right?"

128
00:06:54.058 --> 00:06:55.459
Jack didn't say anything.

129
00:06:55.479 --> 00:06:58.240
"Do I have to call the coach and ask him?"

130
00:06:58.720 --> 00:06:59.420
his mother said.

131
00:07:00.481 --> 00:07:01.281
Jack sighed.

132
00:07:01.301 --> 00:07:05.043
"I'm sorry, Mom," he mumbled.

133
00:07:05.063 --> 00:07:07.664
"I skipped the last three practices.

134
00:07:08.244 --> 00:07:09.845
I went to a coffee shop instead."

135
00:07:11.045 --> 00:07:13.086
Jack's mother didn't seem to know what to say.

136
00:07:13.106 --> 00:07:16.287
"Obviously, we have some things to discuss later."

137
00:07:16.307 --> 00:07:20.445
"Sorry!" Laura mouthed at Jack.

138
00:07:21.445 --> 00:07:23.347
She looked just as confused as Mrs.

139
00:07:23.387 --> 00:07:30.270
Gibson. "My little Tommy would never lie to his mother or skip practice," Mrs.

140
00:07:30.330 --> 00:07:31.271
Wilson chimed in.

141
00:07:31.291 --> 00:07:34.853
"Young man, you should be ashamed."

142
00:07:35.954 --> 00:07:37.555
Jack was ashamed.

143
00:07:38.175 --> 00:07:39.936
But this was his mother's fault too.

144
00:07:40.756 --> 00:07:46.219
She and his father had taken Jack away from his friends and his school and his swimming team

145
00:07:46.259 --> 00:07:49.045
in Oklahoma, where Jack had been a star.

146
00:07:50.126 --> 00:07:56.851
Jack had lied, but so had his parents—about his new bedroom and how great life in California would

147
00:07:56.871 --> 00:07:59.633
be. Anger washed over Jack.

148
00:08:00.354 --> 00:08:03.456
He felt angry at everyone: his parents for the move.

149
00:08:03.996 --> 00:08:05.397
Laura for tattling on him.

150
00:08:05.838 --> 00:08:07.659
Mrs. Wilson for being a busybody.

151
00:08:08.700 --> 00:08:12.723
And his little brother, who announced loudly, "I'm peeing in the pool!"
